  {
   "sid": "s3",
   "date": "2026-09-16",
   "url": "https://www.murray.senate.gov/at-help-hearing-murray-grills-trump-nominees-on-ai-denying-seniors-health-care-abortion-bans-killing-women/",
   "text": "First, you know that you and I very strongly agree about prior authorization being used appropriately and it has in fact largely not been used appropriately in this country. And that undermines trust between providers and patients. In fact, one of my family members who’s here today recently went through a six-week prior authorization stall that was incredibly frustrating at a time of great uncertainty. That is the very thing that must be eliminated. At the same time, it is an appropriate utilization management tool if it is used precisely, and surgically, and appropriately.",
   "source_type": "official_statement",
   "attribution": {
    "kind": "personal",
    "speaker": "Chris Klomp",
    "organization_id": "hhs",
    "basis": "local_span",
    "note": "Chris Klomp answers questions about prior authorization and oversight. The questioner’s allegations do not establish Klomp’s own views."
   },
